index 0000000..6497f0d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/SOLUTION.md
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+# Solution
+
+Two bugs in `lrucache/cache.py`:
+
+1. **`get` did not refresh recency.** A cache hit returned the value without
+   calling `move_to_end(key)`, so reading an entry left it in its original
+   insertion position and it could be evicted as if it were least recently
+   used. Fixed by moving the key to the MRU end of the `OrderedDict` on every
+   valid (non-expired) hit.
+
+2. **`put` evicted on updates to existing keys.** The eviction check was
+   `len(self._data) >= self.capacity` with no regard for whether the key was
+   already present, so overwriting an existing key in a full cache wrongly
+   evicted the LRU entry (shrinking the cache below capacity). Fixed by only
+   evicting when the key is *not* already in the cache — an in-place update
+   never changes the entry count.
